      "content": "#define _GNU_SOURCE\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\n\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  return bodies;\n}\n\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n}\n\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\n  int nbodies;\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\n\n  // Convert AoS input to SoA arrays for cache-friendly access.\n  size_t arr_bytes = (size_t)nbodies * sizeof(float);\n  float *restrict x;\n  float *restrict y;\n  float *restrict z;\n  float *restrict vx;\n  float *restrict vy;\n  float *restrict vz;\n\n  if (posix_memalign((void **)&x, 64, arr_bytes) != 0 ||\n      posix_memalign((void **)&y, 64, arr_bytes) != 0 ||\n      posix_memalign((void **)&z, 64, arr_bytes) != 0 ||\n      posix_memalign((void **)&vx, 64, arr_bytes) != 0 ||\n      posix_memalign((void **)&vy, 64, arr_bytes) != 0 ||\n      posix_memalign((void **)&vz, 64, arr_bytes) != 0) {\n    perror(\"aligned alloc\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n    x[i] = bodies[i].x;\n    y[i] = bodies[i].y;\n    z[i] = bodies[i].z;\n    vx[i] = bodies[i].vx;\n    vy[i] = bodies[i].vy;\n    vz[i] = bodies[i].vz;\n  }\n\n  // Single parallel region spans all iterations to reuse the thread team.\n  #pragma omp parallel\n  {\n    for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; ++iter) {\n      // Compute gravitational forces and update velocities.\n      // Static scheduling preserves exact per-body accumulation order;\n      // SIMD is intentionally not used here to avoid reassociating sums.\n      #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n      for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n        float xi = x[i];\n        float yi = y[i];\n        float zi = z[i];\n        float fx = 0.0f;\n        float fy = 0.0f;\n        float fz = 0.0f;\n\n        int j = 0;\n        // Manual unroll by 4, preserving exact per-j accumulation order.\n        for (; j + 3 < nbodies; j += 4) {\n          float dx0 = x[j] - xi;\n          float dy0 = y[j] - yi;\n          float dz0 = z[j] - zi;\n          float d0 = dx0*dx0 + dy0*dy0 + dz0*dz0 + SOFTENING;\n          float inv0 = 1 / sqrt(d0);\n          float inv30 = inv0 * inv0 * inv0;\n          fx += dx0 * inv30;\n          fy += dy0 * inv30;\n          fz += dz0 * inv30;\n\n          float dx1 = x[j+1] - xi;\n          float dy1 = y[j+1] - yi;\n          float dz1 = z[j+1] - zi;\n          float d1 = dx1*dx1 + dy1*dy1 + dz1*dz1 + SOFTENING;\n          float inv1 = 1 / sqrt(d1);\n          float inv31 = inv1 * inv1 * inv1;\n          fx += dx1 * inv31;\n          fy += dy1 * inv31;\n          fz += dz1 * inv31;\n\n          float dx2 = x[j+2] - xi;\n          float dy2 = y[j+2] - yi;\n          float dz2 = z[j+2] - zi;\n          float d2 = dx2*dx2 + dy2*dy2 + dz2*dz2 + SOFTENING;\n          float inv2 = 1 / sqrt(d2);\n          float inv32 = inv2 * inv2 * inv2;\n          fx += dx2 * inv32;\n          fy += dy2 * inv32;\n          fz += dz2 * inv32;\n\n          float dx3 = x[j+3] - xi;\n          float dy3 = y[j+3] - yi;\n          float dz3 = z[j+3] - zi;\n          float d3 = dx3*dx3 + dy3*dy3 + dz3*dz3 + SOFTENING;\n          float inv3 = 1 / sqrt(d3);\n          float inv33 = inv3 * inv3 * inv3;\n          fx += dx3 * inv33;\n          fy += dy3 * inv33;\n          fz += dz3 * inv33;\n        }\n        for (; j < nbodies; ++j) {\n          float dx = x[j] - xi;\n          float dy = y[j] - yi;\n          float dz = z[j] - zi;\n          float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n          float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n          float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n          fx += dx * inv_dist3;\n          fy += dy * inv_dist3;\n          fz += dz * inv_dist3;\n        }\n\n        vx[i] += DT*fx;\n        vy[i] += DT*fy;\n        vz[i] += DT*fz;\n      }\n\n      // Update positions using the newly computed velocities.\n      // Elementwise and independent, so SIMD is safe here.\n      #pragma omp for simd schedule(static) aligned(x,y,z,vx,vy,vz:64)\n      for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n        x[i] += vx[i] * DT;\n        y[i] += vy[i] * DT;\n        z[i] += vz[i] * DT;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Convert SoA results back to the required AoS output layout.\n  for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n    bodies[i].x = x[i];\n    bodies[i].y = y[i];\n    bodies[i].z = z[i];\n    bodies[i].vx = vx[i];\n    bodies[i].vy = vy[i];\n    bodies[i].vz = vz[i];\n  }\n\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\n\n  free(x); free(y); free(z); free(vx); free(vy); free(vz);\n  free(bodies);\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Combining B's 64-byte aligned allocations and SIMD-friendly position update with A's SoA layout, restrict qualifiers, manual unrolling of the force loop, and C's single persistent OpenMP parallel region will reduce memory latency and vectorize the elementwise phase without perturbing exact floating-point summation order in the force computation.",
  "notes": "The force loop deliberately avoids omp simd to preserve the exact per-body accumulation order required for byte-identical output. The position-update loop is independent and can safely use omp for simd with aligned clauses. posix_memalign provides 64-byte alignment, and _GNU_SOURCE ensures its declaration.",
